# anvil RPC endpoint (the Aave deploy scripts are hardcoded to localhost:8545)
RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545

# Which keys own the chain. Account index 0 is the deployer: Aave's POOL_ADMIN, GMX's
# CONFIG_KEEPER, the owner of every seeded LP position, the holder of the genesis Trove's eUSD --
# and, because every address here is CREATE(deployer, nonce), the account that decides where all of
# them land.
#
# The default below is anvil's public test mnemonic. It is right for local development and CI, and
# wrong for any chain that accepts transactions from participants: those words are printed in
# anvil's banner, so "the deployer" would be a key everyone already holds (issue #74).
#
# For a production chain, put a secret mnemonic here -- this file's sibling `.env` is gitignored,
# so it does not reach the repository -- or keep it out of the filesystem entirely:
#
#   MNEMONIC="$(cat ~/.ascon-secret-mnemonic)" npm run deploy -- --keep-fresh
#
# Whichever you choose, `npm run anvil` and `npm run deploy` have to agree: both read this value,
# and a deploy that finds an anvil holding different keys fails fast rather than half-deploying.
# See "Deploying with a secret mnemonic" in README.md.
MNEMONIC="test test test test test test test test test test test junk"

# Set to true to have the deployer manage the anvil lifecycle (start/stop) itself.
# Set to false if anvil is already running in a separate terminal via `npm run anvil`.
MANAGE_ANVIL=true
